🚀 Why this is optimal?

We only loop once through the array (O(n)).

HashMap insert & get are O(1) average case.

No need for extra visited[] or nested loops.

👉 If your array is very large or contains big numbers, HashMap is the best choice.
👉 If the numbers are small & bounded (e.g., 1–100), you can also use a counting array for even faster performance.

